:zc_settings_debug_log_plug:
> **Yes** also writes a debug log, `/var/log/zfs.master.debug.log`: the commands the plugin runs, how each ended and how long it took, and the name of each request to its admin page.
> Turn it on to reproduce a problem, make the diagnostics zip, then turn it off again.
>
> - A replication and a rewrite run their copy or rewrite commands outside the debug log, and log their own lines in `/var/log/zfs.master.log` whether this is on or not.
> - On a server receiving copies, a sender's requests run outside the debug log too: `/var/log/zfs.master.log` has each copy received or failed, and each request refused.
> - The rsync that copies a folder into a dataset, and a diagnostics run's own commands, are in neither log.
> - The arguments of rsync, and of a command that loads a key or names where one is kept, are left out.
> - Each log keeps about 1 MB at most, its oldest lines going first. A diagnostics zip holds both.
