<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Datasets)_</summary>

_(Dataset Exclusion Pattern)_:
: <textarea name="exclusion" cols="40" rows="1" placeholder="/dockerfiles/.*"><?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['dataset_exclusion'])?></textarea> <span id="zfsm-exclusion-warning" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_datasets_exclusion_plug:
> Hides datasets whose names match this regular expression, with their child datasets, their snapshots and any matching folders. Leave it empty to hide nothing.
>
> - `/docker` hides every dataset with `/docker` in its name, such as `cache/system/docker`.
> - It is one pattern: join several with `|`, such as `/docker|/vms`.
> - Case is ignored. A `.` matches any character, so write `\.` for a dot.
> - A pattern with `%` is read as a Lua pattern, the format older versions used: there a dot is `%.`, `|` is a plain character, and case counts.
>
> A pattern that isn't valid is ignored, and the Main tab says so.
:end

_(Directory Listing)_:
: <textarea name="directory_listing" cols="40" rows="10" placeholder="mypool/docker&#10;mypool/otherdataset"><?=zfsmHtml(implode(PHP_EOL, $zfsm_cfg['directory_listing']))?></textarea>

:zc_settings_directory_listing_plug:
> One dataset name per line, such as `cache/appdata`. The Main tab then lists the folders directly inside each one, with a menu to move or rename each folder; with **Destructive Mode** on, also to convert it into a dataset or delete it.
:end


