<details class="zfsm-section" open markdown="1">
<summary>_(Replication)_</summary>

_(Accept Replicas Into)_:
: <input type="text" name="replica_accept" value="<?=zfsmHtml($zfsm_cfg['replica_accept'])?>" placeholder="off"> <span id="zfsm-replica-accept-warning" style="color:#e22828"></span>

:zc_settings_replica_accept_plug:
> Lets other servers running ZFS Master NG send copies of their datasets here. To set it up:
>
> 1. Create the dataset the copies go into, such as `backup/replicas` (Main, **Create Dataset** on its pool), type its name here and Apply. A pool's top dataset isn't accepted.
> 2. On the sending server, open ZFS Master NG's Settings and add this server under **Add A Server**. Compare the host key it reads with **This Server's Host Key** below, tick that they match, then Add.
> 3. The sender then shows one line under this server's name. Copy it unchanged into this server's Users, root, **SSH authorized keys**, and Apply there. Unraid 6.9 has no such field: add the line to `/boot/config/ssh/root/authorized_keys` instead.
> 4. Press Test beside this server on the sender. It makes the sender's own dataset inside this one, and shows its name.
>
> That line lets the sender's key only list, check and receive copies inside its own dataset here: it can't destroy, roll back or replace anything, or run anything else. Paste it unchanged: the sender's key on a line without these limits, such as the key alone, can run anything as root here.
> Copies never mount or show as block devices, and run with setuid, devices and exec off. A quota on this dataset caps the space all copies use. Leave this empty to accept none.
:end

_(This Server's Host Key)_:
: <span id="zfsm-replica-hostkey"><?=zfsmHtml(zfsmHostKeyFingerprint() ?? 'could not be read')?></span>

:zc_settings_replica_hostkey_plug:
> The fingerprint of this server's SSH host key. A server adding this one reads the key over the network and shows its fingerprint: if the two differ, something else is answering at this server's address, so don't add it.
:end

_(Sender Keys)_:
: <span id="zfsm-replica-keys"><?=zfsmReplicaKeysHtml(zfsmReplicaKeys())?></span>

:zc_settings_replica_keys_plug:
> The lines in root's SSH authorized keys that run replica-serve.php, which receives copies here. A line limits its key to replication only when it has all three:
>
> - `restrict`, and none of `pty`, `port-forwarding`, `agent-forwarding`, `x11-forwarding` or `user-rc`: each gives back something `restrict` takes away.
> - `from=` with the sender's exact IP addresses, commas between several: no ranges, wildcards, `!` or host names.
> - `command=` with exactly `/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zfs.master/scripts/replica-serve.php`, a space and the sender's name.
>
> A line shown in red lacks one of these: replace it with the line the sender shows, unchanged.
:end

</details>

